j-place-lower = a place on the part
j-anchor-inferred = inferred under the cursor
j-anchor-inferred-hint = Hover the part: a face gives its centre, an edge its midpoint (a circular one gives the hole centre), an edge end gives a vertex. No need to declare the kind of anchor up front.

jt-flip-axis = Flip the axis
jt-flip-axis-hint = Turn the primary axis of the first anchor by 180°. The mating side is then chosen anew.
jt-swap-roles = Swap roles
jt-swap-roles-hint = The two sides of a mate are not equal: the solver moves the part of the second anchor. Swapping roles changes which part stays and which one travels.

jp-at-limit = at the stop
jp-at-limit-hint = The degree of freedom has hit its limit. The value does not go past the stop — this is not a failure but the bound you set.

jp-apply-limit = Apply limit position
jp-apply-limit-hint = Put the degree of freedom exactly on its stop. A mechanism with limits is inspected at its extremes — that is where it meets its neighbour.
jp-limit-upper = to the upper stop
jp-limit-lower = to the lower stop

j-fault-anchor-on-moving-part = anchor on a moving part
j-fault-anchor-on-moving-part-hint = The anchor is declared on this assembly but takes its geometry from a part that travels inside it. Such an anchor moves away every time that part moves, and the assembly can never settle. Re-pick the anchor on stationary geometry — or mate the moving part directly.

j-anchor-on-moving-part-refused = This geometry belongs to a part that travels inside the chosen assembly: an anchor on it would move away with the part and the assembly would never settle. Point at stationary geometry — or mate the moving part directly.

in-assembly-tool-cancelled = Assembly tool cancelled

jp-grounded-inside-moving = grounded inside a moving assembly: { $list }
jp-grounded-inside-moving-hint = These parts are grounded but sit inside a subassembly driven by a mate: they hold still relative to their neighbours yet travel with the assembly. If you need them fixed in the world, ground the assembly itself.

