cmd-thread-mate-external = Cut on a shaft Ø{ $own } mm. The mating part: an internal thread, same size and pitch, in a hole Ø{ $mate } mm.
cmd-thread-mate-internal = Drill the hole Ø{ $own } mm. The mating part: an external thread, same size and pitch, on a shaft Ø{ $mate } mm.
cmd-thread-mate-hint = The counterpart takes the same standard, size, pitch, number of starts, hand and fit — only the side differs. The fit is one value for the pair: it thins the external thread and thickens the internal one.

cmd-thread-too-wide = The groove is { $width } mm wide and the pitch is only { $pitch }: the turns overlap and eat one another. Reduce the depth to { $depth } mm, or raise the pitch to { $minpitch }.

cmd-thread-fit-capped = A clearance of { $asked } mm does not fit this pitch: { $given } mm is used. The groove cannot be wider than the pitch. For the rest, take a coarser pitch, or turn the shaft down (open the hole up) by { $rest } mm.

